        "category": "performance",
        "title": "Concurrent thread total can still exceed machine_cores after scaling",
        "explanation": "All regions are now prefaulted concurrently in one scope (previously sequentially, max 16 threads at a time). The cap rescales each region with cmp::max(1, threads * machine_cores / total), so every non-empty region keeps at least one thread. With more non-empty regions than cores (e.g. 6 regions on a 4-core / cgroup-limited host), more threads than cores run at once, all contending on mmap_lock and the hugetlb/page allocator locks. This defeats the stated budget.",
        "suggestion": "Enforce the budget exactly, e.g. distribute machine_cores with largest-remainder rounding, or when regions outnumber cores, process the excess regions in a later batch instead of flooring each to 1.",
        "evidence": "            plan.threads = cmp::max(1, plan.threads * machine_cores / total);",
        "confidence": 0.55,
        "id": "93333e1793fd",
